<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Franco-Thai War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1940">1940</a>–<a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as French–Thai War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Franco-Thai War was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">French Indochina</a> from late 1940 to early 1941 over territories that Siam had ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> decades earlier. The French navy won at Ko Chang in January 1941, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> imposed a settlement, confirmed by a treaty in Tokyo in May 1941, that transferred parts of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a> to Thailand until 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/franco-thai-war.jpg" alt="Franco-Thai War" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giuseppe Rava · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_Between_the_Army_of_Thailand_and_the_French_Army.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
